ess Leia Organa and General Han…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/star-wars/resistance/rey\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Used By\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Rey</strong>\n                    <span>Rey Skywalker, also known simply as Rey, was a Jedi member of the Resistance during the war against the First Order. The human woman was a scavenger on the planet Jakku, but her life was changed by tumultuous events in…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/star-wars/sith\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Used By\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Sith</strong>\n                    <span>The Sith, also referred to as the Sith Order, was an ancient religious order of Force-wielders devoted to the dark side of the Force. Driven by their raw emotions, including hate, anger, and greed, the Sith were…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars/rebel-alliance/luke-skywalker\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Luke Skywalker\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Luke is a Jedi sensitive to the Force.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars/resistance/rey\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Rey\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Rey is powerfully Force-sensitive.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars/sith\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Sith\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Sith wield the dark side of the Force.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars/jedi-order\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Jedi Order\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Jedi serve the light side of the Force.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars/grogu\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Grogu\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Grogu is Force-sensitive.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Connected To</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Connected To\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/star-wars\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Star Wars\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>The Force is central to Star Wars mythology.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>The Force is also referenced as Force.</li><li>The Force is central to Star Wars mythology.</li><li>Luke is a Jedi sensitive to the Force.</li><li>Rey is powerfully Force-sensitive.</li><li>Sith wield the dark side of the Force.</li><li>Evidence around The Force is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"sources\">\n    <h2>Sources &amp; further reading</h2>\n    <p><a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/The_Force\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Fandom wiki</a></p>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is The Force?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        The Force was an energy field created by all life that bound everything in the universe together. It was known by a variety of names throughout galactic history. It was called the Ashla by the Lasats, the Life Current by the Mustafarians, the Tide by the Lew&#039;elans, the Sight by the Chiss, the Life Wind by the Zeffonians, the Great Presence by the Pathfinders of the Chaos, the Luminous Mist by the Mist-Weavers, the Unity by the Sorcerers of Tund, the Beyond by the Magys and her people, the Thread by the Brendok coven of witches, the Road of All Moons by the exogorths or simply It by the dianoga Omi. On Metagos it was known as the the Web. The Force was created by life, and therefore it resided in all life forms. It was especially powerful in a select group of individuals who were born with a high concentration of midi-chlorians&amp;mdash;microscopic, intelligent lifeforms that formed a symbiotic relationship with and communicated the will of the Force to their host and resided within all living cells. These people were deemed Force-sensitive, and were capable of consciously sensing the Force. With this conscious sense of the Force came the ability to harness it, allowing Force-sensitives to access various Force powers. Unlike organic beings, droids and other artificial constructs existed outside of the Force. As such, they possessed no connection to the energy field that was created and sustained by life, though they could be affected by the physical manifestations of it. Apart from its scientific aspect, the Force was the basis of various religious organizations, who held differing views as to the nature and purpose of the Force. These included the Church of the Force, the Guardians of the Whills, and most notably the Jedi and <a href=\"/star-wars/sith\" class=\"entity-link\">Sith</a> Orders. In addition, the Lasats believed that the Force was the &quot;spirit&quot; of the galaxy.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The Force as a recorded concept existed for well over twenty-five thousand years. There were two overarching and symbiotic aspects of the Force. The Living Force was the energy of all life, which, in turn, fed into the Cosmic Force&amp;mdash;which bound everything together and communicated the will of the Force through the midi-chlorians. The Jedi followed a code of selflessness and service to others; therefore, they adhered to the light side of the Force, one of two methods of using the all-encompassing energy field. The Jedi&#039;s adversaries, the <a href=\"/star-wars/sith\" class=\"entity-link\">Sith</a>, coveted strength and power through the dark side of the Force. Their opposing philosophies led to millennia of cyclical conflict between the two orders, which resulted in both the extinction of the <a href=\"/star-wars/sith\" class=\"entity-link\">Sith</a> and the near annihilation of the Jedi.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Force.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":1243,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"0787d328-0cf1-40d7-8b80-19cc49c2c3ea","name":"The Force","slug":"the-force","type":"concept","kind":"concept","type_label":"Concept","short_description":"The Force was an energy field created by all life that bound everything in the universe together. It was known by a variety of names throughout galactic history. It was called the Ashla by the Lasats, the Life Current…","description":"The Force was an energy field created by all life that bound everything in the universe together. It was known by a variety of names throughout galactic history. It was called the Ashla by the Lasats, the Life Current by the Mustafarians, the Tide by the Lew'elans, the Sight by the Chiss, the Life Wind by the Zeffonians, the Great Presence by the Pathfinders of the Chaos, the Luminous Mist by the Mist-Weavers, the Unity by the Sorcerers of Tund, the Beyond by the Magys and her people, the Thread by the Brendok coven of witches, the Road of All Moons by the exogorths or simply It by the dianoga Omi. On Metagos it was known as the the Web. The Force was created by life, and therefore it resided in all life forms. It was especially powerful in a select group of individuals who were born with a high concentration of midi-chlorians&mdash;microscopic, intelligent lifeforms that formed a symbiotic relationship with and communicated the will of the Force to their host and resided within all living cells. These people were deemed Force-sensitive, and were capable of consciously sensing the Force. With this conscious sense of the Force came the ability to harness it, allowing Force-sensitives to access various Force powers. Unlike organic beings, droids and other artificial constructs existed outside of the Force. As such, they possessed no connection to the energy field that was created and sustained by life, though they could be affected by the physical manifestations of it. Apart from its scientific aspect, the Force was the basis of various religious organizations, who held differing views as to the nature and purpose of the Force. These included the Church of the Force, the Guardians of the Whills, and most notably the Jedi and Sith Orders. In addition, the Lasats believed that the Force was the \"spirit\" of the galaxy.\n\nThe Force as a recorded concept existed for well over twenty-five thousand years. There were two overarching and symbiotic aspects of the Force. The Living Force was the energy of all life, which, in turn, fed into the Cosmic Force&mdash;which bound everything together and communicated the will of the Force through the midi-chlorians. The Jedi followed a code of selflessness and service to others; therefore, they adhered to the light side of the Force, one of two methods of using the all-encompassing energy field. The Jedi's adversaries, the Sith, coveted strength and power through the dark side of the Force. Their opposing philosophies led to millennia of cyclical conflict between the two orders, which resulted in both the extinction of the Sith and the near annihilation of the Jedi.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"star-wars","aliases":["Force","The Force"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/f7/YodaForceLift.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/360?cb=20070711224710","image_source":"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/The_Force","image_credit":"Fair-use identification thumbnail via Wookieepedia (Star Wars Fandom). Character / franchise art © Lucasfilm Ltd. / Disney (as applicable). Not free or redistributable artwork.","image_license":"fair_use","image_usage":"fair_use_identification","image_alt":"Identification thumbnail for The Force"},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"star-wars","title":"STAR WARS is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"STAR WARS and all related characters, names, marks, and images are trademarks of Lucasfilm Ltd. and/or Disney. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational pr